text.extend(['', 'Hingant-Yvinec: arXiv:1609.00697 (2016 preprint), PDF downloaded. Section 3 deals with Becker-Doring monomer attachment/removal; these are different transitions. The survey references the stationary work of Durrett et al.; it provides no identified solution of the present spectral-gap order.','', 'Hoze-Holcman: arXiv:1611.06493 (2016 preprint; later Annals of Applied Probability paper above), PDF downloaded. Stationary probabilities, moments and tagged-particle meeting/separation times are treated. Mean tagged-particle times are not spectral relaxation times; no matching relaxation-order theorem identified in the text.','', 'Other arXiv leads: 2208.10699, Double Coset Markov Chains (Diaconis, Ram, Simper), uses permutation/double-coset coagulation-fragmentation chains, not this per-link linear-polymer chain; 1612.07036, Analytical results for a coagulation/decoagulation model on an inhomogeneous lattice, is a spatial lattice reaction model; 0811.1169 treats a deterministic Smoluchowski equation. None is an exact solution in print of P0211. The remaining returned titles and metadata remain saved in arxiv*.xml and crossref*.json; astrophysics, continuum PDE and species-sampling duality hits are off model.','', 'GitHub repository query returned numerical PDE, species-sampling and clustering implementations (github.json); none supplied a matching proved theorem.','', '## Every network query / fetch','', 'The initial source-page fetch was https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/~aldous/Research/OP/coag_frag.html on 2026-10-11, successful, saved as source.html. The following are the exact additional request URLs and outcomes:',''])
